# Named camera-sensor colorimetry: PBRT-v4's PixelSensor non-default path
# ("nikon_d850", "canon_eos_100d", "canon_eos_5d_mkiv"), used by explosion,
# bunny-cloud, clouds, zero-day, dambreak, pbrt-book, and crown. Data ported
# verbatim from pbrt-v4's src/pbrt/util/spectrum.cpp (named sensor r/g/b
# curves, CIE daylight-illuminant S0/S1/S2 basis) and src/pbrt/film.cpp (the
# 24 Macbeth ColorChecker swatch reflectances, Danny Pascale/BabelColor data)
# via scratchpad/sensor_port/extract.py.
#
# Design: pbrt's PixelSensor integrates each hero-wavelength radiance sample
# against the sensor's MEASURED r/g/b response curves (not CIE X/Y/Z), then
# maps that raw camera RGB through a 3x3 matrix fit via least-squares against
# 24 calibration swatches lit by the whitebalance-temperature CIE daylight
# illuminant. Rather than threading three more spectral-context pointers and
# a sensor-mode flag through every CPU/GPU/wavefront call site that touches
# cie_x/y/z (dozens, across bdpt_*.mojo/sppm.mojo/shading.mojo/gpu_media.mojo),
# this exploits a fact verified by grepping every one of those call sites:
# cie_x/y/z are passed around everywhere but only ever DEREFERENCED in one
# place, spectrum.mojo's spectral_sample_to_rgb (via cie_xyz_at_ptr) — the
# final radiance-to-RGB step. Every other site (spec_refl, spec_illum,
# _eval_vertex_spectral, medium_sigma_t_spectral, ...) threads the pointers
# through unused; they only touch spectral_coeffs/res/d65 (the RGB<->spectral
# upsampling table, a completely separate mechanism).
#
# So: for a supported named sensor, gonzales substitutes the sensor's own
# r/g/b response curves (resampled onto the same 95-sample CIE_LAMBDA_MIN..
# CIE_LAMBDA_MAX grid) for the CieXyzTables x/y/z tables at scene-load time.
# spectral_sample_to_rgb's per-sample math is then integrating the sensor's
# real response, unmodified, at zero extra per-sample cost, still through the
# SAME /CIE_Y_INTEGRAL normalization and CIE XYZ->sRGB matrix gonzales always
# applies -- that normalization is gonzales's own per-sample convention
# (matching pbrt's SampledSpectrum::ToXYZ, calibrated so the default cie1931
# sensor's brightness matches pbrt), not part of pbrt's real PixelSensor
# pipeline, and it is IDENTICAL on both sides of the substitution below, so
# it never needs to be undone -- only the sensor's colour-response SHAPE
# does. named_sensor_srgb_matrix's returned matrix, installed in place of
# _film_white_balance_matrix's result and applied the same way (by
# apply_film_sensor, once per pixel, post-render), corrects exactly that:
#
#   Let S = the fixed XYZ->sRGB matrix spectral_sample_to_rgb applies.
#   Let F = XYZFromSensorRGB, this file's least-squares fit (unit-preserving:
#   both calibration sides, rgbCamera and xyzOutput, are independently
#   g_integral-normalized the same way pbrt normalizes them).
#   Accumulated buffer:  buf = S @ (raw_sensor_rgb / CIE_Y_INTEGRAL)
#   Desired final:       out = S @ F @ (raw_sensor_rgb / CIE_Y_INTEGRAL)
#                            = (S @ F @ inv(S)) @ buf
#
# named_sensor_srgb_matrix returns exactly WB = S @ F @ inv(S), in the same
# row-major SIMD[DType.float32,16] convention apply_film_sensor already
# expects. No render-hot-path function or call site is touched.
#
# Sanity check this derivation must pass (and does): feed the exact CIE X/Y/Z
# matching functions in as a fake "sensor" and run the whole calibration --
# F must come out ~= Identity (a "sensor" whose response IS the CIE curves
# should reproduce plain cie1931 rendering exactly), so WB must come out
# ~= Identity too, not CIE_Y_INTEGRAL*Identity. An earlier version of this
# file multiplied WB by CIE_Y_INTEGRAL, which passed every OTHER check
# (an independent from-scratch Python re-derivation matched it bit-for-bit)
# but failed exactly this self-check and rendered explosion.pbrt ~161x too
# bright -- the bug was invisible to a from-scratch cross-check because
# that check reproduced the same wrong premise, not the actual pbrt pipeline.

from std.math import exp
from gonzales.rgb2spec import (
    _CIE_X, _CIE_Y, _CIE_Z, _CIE_D65_RAW, _cie_interp, _cie_d65,
    CIE_LAMBDA_MIN, CIE_LAMBDA_MAX, CIE_SAMPLES,
    _XYZ_TO_SRGB00, _XYZ_TO_SRGB01, _XYZ_TO_SRGB02,
    _XYZ_TO_SRGB10, _XYZ_TO_SRGB11, _XYZ_TO_SRGB12,
    _XYZ_TO_SRGB20, _XYZ_TO_SRGB21, _XYZ_TO_SRGB22,
)

# AUTO-EXTRACTED from pbrt-v4 src/pbrt/util/spectrum.cpp and film.cpp.
# Do not hand-edit; regenerate via scratchpad/sensor_port/extract.py.

